  "description": "Recounts Sinuhe’s flight during the royal succession, his success in Retjenu, his duel, the king’s pardon and his return for an Egyptian burial. Examines the tension between a flourishing life abroad and courtly belonging, the work’s fictional autobiographical voice, royal ideology and ma’at, and the papyrus and ostraca witnesses through which scribes transmitted it.",
